BRD-Gen: Product Requirements Document
Version: 1.0 | Context: 24-hour hackathon (HackSprint) | Status: Ready to build

1. Problem statement
Build a scalable, multi-modal AI system using Google Gemini AI and integrated Google Cloud tools (Vertex AI, Cloud Storage, BigQuery) that can process real-time, fragmented data (text, images, documents) and deliver accurate, context-aware, and explainable decisions in complex and dynamic environments.

Our domain choice: business requirements gathering.

The pain: requirements for a project are scattered across meeting notes, emails, chats, whiteboard photos and PDFs. Analysts stitch them together by hand, which takes days, misses contradictions, and leaves no trace of who asked for what.

2. Product vision
BRD-Gen is an AI agent that reads fragmented, multi-modal project inputs and produces a Business Requirements Document in which every requirement shows its source, and every contradiction is flagged for a human.

How it maps to the problem statement
Problem statement says	BRD-Gen delivers
Multi-modal, fragmented data	Text, image and PDF inputs combined per project
Real-time	New inputs update the requirement set without starting over
Context-aware	Requirements are judged against all sources, not one file
Explainable decisions	Each requirement shows source, confidence and conflicts
Accurate	Writer sees only extracted, source-linked requirements
Scalable, Google Cloud	Serverless design using Gemini, Cloud Storage, BigQuery
3. Users
User	Need
Business analyst (primary)	Turn scattered inputs into a clean BRD fast
Project manager / stakeholder	Confirm requirements, resolve conflicts, approve
Reviewer / auditor	See where each requirement came from
4. Goals and non-goals
Goals (hackathon):

Upload mixed files and get a structured list of requirements with sources.
Detect and show at least one contradiction between sources.
Generate a downloadable BRD with a traceability table.
Use Gemini plus at least Cloud Storage and BigQuery.
Non-goals (future scope, show on roadmap only):

Live audio transcription, Jira export, multi-user login, Dataflow streaming, fine-tuning, full Vector Search.
5. Scope
Priority	Feature
Must (MVP)	File upload, Gemini extraction, source references, conflict detection, BRD generation, traceability table, download
Should	Cloud Storage for uploads, BigQuery for requirements, approve/reject per requirement, confidence display
Could	Regenerate only changed sections, gap questions ("what is missing?"), DOCX export
Won't (this round)	Authentication, real-time streaming pipeline, integrations
6. Functional requirements
ID	Requirement	Priority	Acceptance criteria
FR-01	The user can upload multiple files (.txt, .md, .pdf, .png, .jpg)	Must	Three mixed files upload without error
FR-02	The system extracts requirements from every file type, including images	Must	A requirement drawn from a whiteboard photo appears in results
FR-03	Each requirement has an ID, type, text, actor, priority, source and confidence	Must	All fields present in the output table
FR-04	Each requirement cites its source (file plus page or timestamp or region)	Must	No requirement displayed without a source
FR-05	The system flags contradictions between requirements	Must	Planted 5 min vs 15 min conflict is shown in a red banner
FR-06	The system generates a BRD with sections: functional, non-functional, risks, open questions	Must	BRD preview renders all four sections
FR-07	The BRD includes a traceability table (requirement, source, confidence)	Must	Table matches the requirements list
FR-08	The user can download the BRD (Markdown at minimum)	Must	Downloaded file opens correctly
FR-09	Raw files are stored in Cloud Storage	Should	Uploaded file visible in the bucket
FR-10	Requirements and conflicts are stored in BigQuery	Should	Rows queryable in BigQuery
FR-11	The user can approve or reject each requirement	Should	Rejected items disappear from the BRD
FR-12	The system lists open questions where information is missing	Could	At least one question generated for a thin input
FR-13	Adding a new file updates the existing requirement set	Could	New requirements merge with the old ones
7. Non-functional requirements
ID	Requirement	Target
NFR-01	Accuracy: no invented requirements	Every requirement traces to a real source text
NFR-02	Explainability	Source, confidence and conflict flag on every item
NFR-03	Performance	Three small files processed in under ~60 seconds
NFR-04	Security	API keys never in code or on slides; no real personal data in demos
NFR-05	Reliability	Clear error message if the API fails; demo mode works offline
NFR-06	Usability	One page, three clicks from upload to download
8. System design summary
Flow: Upload → Cloud Storage → Gemini extraction (structured JSON) → consolidation and conflict check → BigQuery → Gemini BRD writer (only from stored requirements) → verification and human review → BRD plus traceability table.

Tech stack:

Layer	Choice
AI	Gemini (Flash for extraction, Pro for writing) via the Gemini API or Vertex AI
Storage	Cloud Storage (files), BigQuery (requirements, sources, conflicts)
Backend / UI	Python, Streamlit (Cloud Run for scale-up)
Libraries	google-genai, pydantic, pandas
Key design rule: the BRD writer never sees raw files, only the extracted, source-linked requirements. This is what prevents hallucination.

9. Data model
requirements: req_id, project_id, type, text, actor, priority, source, confidence, status sources: source_id, file_name, type, uri, uploaded_at conflicts: conflict_id, req_ids, issue, status open_questions: q_id, section, question

10. Success metrics
Metric	How to measure	Target
Requirement recall	Plant 10 requirements across the files; count how many are found	8 of 10 or better
Traceability	Share of requirements with a valid source	100%
Conflict detection	Planted contradictions caught	1 of 1
Time to first BRD	Upload to download	Under 2 minutes
Report what you actually measure. Do not claim numbers you have not tested.

11. Test plan
Create one demo project ("Loan Portal Revamp") with:

kickoff_call.txt: includes "notify the officer within 15 minutes"
emails.pdf: includes "notify within 5 minutes" and an encryption requirement
whiteboard.jpg: a hand-drawn sketch with a status dashboard
Check: all three files are read, the conflict is flagged, the BRD cites sources, and the download works.

12. Risks
Risk	Mitigation
API quota or Wi-Fi fails during demo	Keep demo mode and a recorded run as backup
Model misses or invents items	Strict JSON schema, temperature 0, source required, manual spot-check
Handwriting or image quality is poor	Use a clear, large-text whiteboard photo
Cloud setup eats time	Build the core first; add Storage and BigQuery after
Scope creep	Freeze scope after the Must list
13. 24-hour plan
Hours	Work
0-2	Setup, API key, repo, run the existing prototype in demo mode
2-6	Live extraction on text, PDF and image; tune the prompt; add sources
6-10	Conflict detection, BRD generation, traceability table
10-14	Cloud Storage and BigQuery integration
14-18	Approve/reject, open questions, UI polish
18-21	Test on the demo project, fix bugs, measure results
21-23	Screenshots, README, record backup demo
23-24	Final check, submit
